# Bundled D2R reference tables are hashed byte-for-byte against the manifest in
# contrib/d2rdoc, and that manifest records them with CRLF endings - the form
# the game itself reads. The blobs are stored LF, so a Windows clone matched
# only because core.autocrlf converted them on checkout while a Linux clone
# produced LF and failed every hash.
#
# Pinning the checkout ending makes every platform materialize the bytes the
# manifest describes. File content and the manifest are both untouched.
contrib/d2rdoc/*/reference/*.txt text eol=crlf
